hi I'm Hannah your friendly neighborhood  wine mom tonight I want to talk about a  topic that I'm often asked not  necessarily in the comments or via text  but just in general life how do I know  that I'm pregnant and this is not about  me being pregnant this is about other  people wanting to know how they know  that they are pregnant not me I am NOT  having any more babies but I didn't  realize how much was in the bottle so  first I just want to say if you are  pregnant and genuinely wondering if you  are pregnant don't watch this video  because you will never know for sure  until you are in the doctor's office you  have gotten a blood test and that blood  test has confirmed that you are in fact  pregnant and also I'm not a doctor or  actually qualified to advise anybody on  anything I just like to drink wine on my  couch and I'm doing pregnant twice well  I got so first how soon can you find out  one thing that I did not realize when I  found out I was pregnant with my first  is that they calculate pregnancy from  the first day of your last period so if  you calculate from the first day of your  last period let's assume two weeks later  you ovulate you can know as soon as a  month after that whether or not you are  pregnant no for those of you who like  have this thought that you can like have  sex and wake up the next morning  realizing that you're pregnant there's  just no way you don't wake up the day  after having sex being like I think I  got pregnant last night it's like a  chalice of wine I will take a small sip  so let's talk about a couple things that  can happen when you take a pregnancy  test you can get false results they can  either give you a false positive or  false negative more typically it's a  false negative false positives are  pretty rare but they happen for example  I had a false positive on a pregnancy  test freaked out then I got my period  but then my period lasted like two weeks  and I was pretty confused because I was  like mentally preparing myself for like  a child and then I get my period and it  turned out to be a chemical pregnancy  which means the egg was fertilized but  it never embedded in the uterine wall  essentially it was releasing the  hormones that said I was pregnant but I  wasn't and then it just occurred like a  normal period  nothing but joy in this episode and also  you can take one and get a negative when  you are totally [ __ ] pregnant man like  you can be just at the very very early  stages of pregnancy and not urine test  does not pick it up enough so home  pregnancy tests are great they're a  great resource it's a great way to calm  your nerves or like figure out what's  happening but ultimately until you're at  that doctor's office getting a positive  yes or no from your doctor you don't  know for sure he's the real fun today  let's drink more so next let's talk  about early pregnancy symptoms there's a  fly in this room and I'm gonna kill it  where'd it go so first of all you might  have some food aversions for no reason  like for example when I was pregnant  with both of my sons at the very  beginning of my pregnancy I just wanted  to drink ranch dressing and that's all I  wanted to have and if this food isn't  drenched in ranch dressing I don't want  to eat it also you might blow a little  bit more than usual  but for me as the person who just like  floats up and down all day long like  that was never an issue next your boobs  might get super sore I remember when I  was pregnant with both of my kids if you  just like took two fingers and tapped  like right on the nipple area it would  not feel good also you might have some  light spotting or bleeding if you are  pregnant and I think a lot of people see  that spotting and either feel relieved  because they're hoping that they weren't  pregnant or feel disappointed because  they were hoping that they were pregnant  and they think that they're starting  their period you can get implantation  spotting which means that the fertilized  egg is implanting into the uterus and it  causes a little bit of bleeding and it's  something that looks like the start of a  period but it actually means that you're  pregnant and then last you're gonna get  some mood swings I remember being like  zero to 60 in two seconds just like  happy to sad for absolutely no reason  I'd see a commercial with puppies in it  and just be like but if all these  symptoms sound familiar and like  something that you've heard before it's  because they're all the same symptoms as  PMS really come on like  really why did the body have to do us  like that like here you go you could  either be getting your period or  pregnant with a child you don't know cuz  it's the same the last you will always  want to know how I found out that I was  pregnant because I've done it a couple  of times so with both of them I  experienced those very very similar PMS  symptoms of like bloating cramping sore  breasts like nausea I ended up taking a  pregnancy test as soon as I missed my  period both times it was positive and  then I went to the doctor and confirmed  but before I took that pregnancy test  and before I missed my period I had this  feeling that I was gonna miss my period  I don't know if it's intuition of your  body but I just knew and I think it says  something because both of my son's I  wasn't necessarily trying to get  pregnant so I wasn't like actively  looking for those signs or like hoping  for those signs  I just knew and this intuition doesn't  come like the day after you have sex  this isn't like a wake up the next day  and like oh my god I'm pregnant  but honestly pregnancy is so different  from mom to Mom I have so many mom  friends and all of our pregnancies and  the way we found out and the way that it  was were polar opposites and I mean in  every direction it is so different so  there's no one way of knowing whether or  not you're pregnant well there's one way  and that's going to the doctor not blood  test so that's all I got for today I'm  Hannah your friendly neighborhood wine  mom and if you have been pregnant and  found out about a pregnancy leave how  you found out in the comments or like  what your symptoms were how you found  out because I'm really curious to read  that and if you have a question or  anything you want me to talk about in  future episodes leave it in the comments  or text me I read all of them and just  remember that I like to give advice but  at the end of the day I'm not a doctor  I'm just a normal mom who drinks wine on  the couch so if you have any real  questions make sure to ask your doctor  he's safe don't take advice from me  [Music]  till next time I don't think I can  finish all this I'm Anika solidus  [Music]

